<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">craft</ansi>

Crafting lets you combine raw materials into useful items — weapons, armor, potions,
and more. You need the right skill, the right ingredients, and in most cases a crafting
station in the room with you.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Basic Usage ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>               Show all known recipes with their status.
  <ansi fg="command">craft</ansi>                    Same as craft list.
  <ansi fg="command">craft <recipe name></ansi>      Start crafting a recipe (partial name works).

Examples:
  <ansi fg="command">craft list</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">craft iron dagger</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">craft healing</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Recipe List ━━━</ansi>

The list shows every recipe your character could potentially learn about, grouped by skill.
Each entry shows a status indicator:

  <ansi fg="green">[V]</ansi>  You can craft this right now (station present, skill met, ingredients in pack).
  <ansi fg="red">[X]</ansi>  Something is blocking the craft (see the reason shown to the right).

Blocking reasons:
  <ansi fg="red">skill N required</ansi>   Your skill level is too low.
  <ansi fg="red">need forge</ansi>         You must be at the right crafting station.
  <ansi fg="red">missing iron-ingot</ansi> You don't have one of the required ingredients.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Starting a Craft ━━━</ansi>

When you start crafting, the work takes several rounds to complete:

  Round 0 (command):  <ansi fg="yellow">You begin crafting Iron Dagger... (3 rounds)</ansi>
  Round 1 (tick):     <ansi fg="yellow">You continue working on iron-dagger... (1/3)</ansi>
  Round 2 (tick):     <ansi fg="yellow">You continue working on iron-dagger... (2/3)</ansi>
  Round 3 (tick):     Success or failure message; item appears in your inventory.

You cannot start crafting while in active combat. If something attacks you mid-craft,
your work is interrupted and you must start over. Your ingredients are NOT consumed on
an interruption — only on a completed attempt (success or failure).

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Success and Failure ━━━</ansi>

When the final round completes, your success chance is:

  50% + (your skill level − recipe minimum) × 5%
  Clamped between 5% and 95%.

At skill 0 crafting a recipe with minimum 0: 50% chance.
At skill 10 with minimum 0: 95% chance (capped).
At skill 0 with minimum 5: 25% chance.

On failure your ingredients are consumed but no item is produced. Higher skill makes
failure rare, but never impossible until 95%.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Crafting Stations ━━━</ansi>

Most recipes require a specific crafting station in the room:

  <ansi fg="yellow">forge</ansi>          Required for blacksmithing recipes. Found in The Forge (east of Town Square).
  <ansi fg="yellow">alchemy_bench</ansi>  Required for alchemy recipes. Found in The Alchemist's Workshop
                   (west of Training Grounds).

The recipe list tells you which station a recipe needs. If you type <ansi fg="command">craft iron dagger</ansi>
from a room with no forge, you will see an error rather than waste your time.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Getting Ingredients ━━━</ansi>

Ingredients are picked up from the floor or looted from mobs, just like any other item.
Look for materials on the ground in crafting station rooms, or kill mobs that carry them:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Cave goblin</ansi>     (The Forge) drops iron ingot + leather strip.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Feral herbalist</ansi> (Workshop)  drops healer's root, bitter thistle, cloth strip.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Rat</ansi>             (Training Grounds) drops leather strip.

Use <ansi fg="command">get <item></ansi> to pick up floor items, <ansi fg="command">inventory</ansi> to check what you are carrying.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help blacksmithing</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help alchemy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help foraging</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help skills</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>

